  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations to Kansas total $2.5B. There were 18,430 awards, with an average award size of $137K, and obligations are down 29.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in the state at $1.5B, followed by the Department of Transportation at $456M and the Department of Defense at $432M. ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. is the single largest vendor, receiving $1.3B in obligations, with INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC. next at $374M. Computer Systems Design Services is the top industry by obligations at $1.3B, while aerospace and air-transportation support categories together account for several of the next largest industry totals, including $373M and $90.4M. Historic context shows FY25 at $3.6B and FY24 at $3.3B, compared with $2.5B in FY26 to date. All figures reported here are contract obligations and the current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 29.7% year over year. FY26 to date obligations are $2.5B, below FY25 obligations of $3.6B and below FY22 obligations of $4.2B. The FY26 to date total matches the partial fiscal-year reporting period and should be read as a fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are obligations concentrated in Kansas?",
        "body": "Obligations are concentrated in a few buyers and vendors. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for $1.5B of obligations, and ORACLE HEALTH GOVERNMENT SERVICES, INC. accounts for $1.3B. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest industry by obligations at $1.3B, followed by the search and detection manufacturing category at $373M."
      }
    ]
  },
